The function $f$ is the characteristic function $\mathbf{1}_{\mathbb{Q}\cap[0,1]}$. The set $\mathbb{Q}\cap[0,1]$ is countable, hence has Lebesgue measure zero. Therefore $\mathbf{1}_{\mathbb{Q}\cap[0,1]}$ is Lebesgue integrable and
\[
\label{eq:8.u162}
\int_{[0,1]} \mathbf{1}_{\mathbb{Q}\cap[0,1]}\,d\mu = \mu(\mathbb{Q}\cap[0,1])=0.
\]
